// December 8 festival cutscene. Kept separate from Cutscene_Prologue for testing.
// The Prologue scene's YarnCutscene Start Node can be set to Dec8_Festival_Cutscene
// in Unity when this version is ready to preview.
// All six pictures already exist in CutsceneCanvas's Pictures list.
// AUDIO TODO: No separate student-chatter or distant-music cues were found;
// festival_crowd is the available festival ambience.
// AUDIO TODO: No quiet sigh cue was found. Add one at the final beat if desired.
// VISUAL TODO: The friends-walking image is a still; no walking animation exists
// for this cutscene. The pause below implies Anin falling behind for now.

title: Dec8_Festival_Cutscene
tags: cutscene festival december8 testing
---
<<ambience_start "festival_crowd">>
<<cutscene_image "cutscene_prologue_1">>
December 8. Our last school festival.

<<cutscene_image "cutscene_prologue_2a">>
Lila: Best festival ever!
Dira: You say that every year.
Kirana: She's not wrong, though.

<<cutscene_image "cutscene_prologue_2b">>
Anin: Haha, yeah. I wish we could do this again.

<<cutscene_image "cutscene_prologue_3a">>
Kirana: Come on! Only three more days until graduation!
// Hold on the still image while the friends move ahead and Anin slows.
<<delay 0.8>>

<<cutscene_image "cutscene_prologue_3b">>
// Muffle the crowd as Anin's attention turns inward.
<<ambience_muffle 1.5>>
Anin: Only three days...

<<cutscene_image "cutscene_prologue_3c">>
Anin: Why does that feel so soon?
// AUDIO TODO: Play a quiet sigh here when its cue is added.
<<ambience_stop 0.8>>
// The Prologue scene behind CutsceneView is black, so closing the image fades to black.
<<cutscene_end>>
===
